  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "unkn_box_read",
    "file": "gpac/src/isomedia/box_code_base.c",
    "description": "The PoV triggers an invalid free due to uninitialized `GF_UnknownBox::data`. In `unkn_box_read`, when an unknown box has zero payload (`bytesToRead == 0`), the function returns early without initializing `ptr->data`/`ptr->dataSize`. Later during teardown, `unkn_box_del` unconditionally checks `if (ptr->data) gf_free(ptr->data);`, so a garbage non-NULL pointer may be freed, causing the ASan crash in `free` (wild pointer read). Crash is observed in `unkn_box_del` via `gf_isom_box_del` recursion, but root cause is missing field initialization in `unkn_box_read`/constructor path for zero-size unknown boxes.",
    "conditions": "Input must create a `uuid`/unknown box parsed as `GF_UnknownBox` with declared size equal to header size (no payload), e.g. the provided 24-byte uuid box. Parsing succeeds with `unkn_box_read` taking the `!bytesToRead` early return path, leaving `data` uninitialized. On `gf_isom_close` -> `gf_isom_delete_movie` cleanup, `gf_isom_box_del` calls `unkn_box_del`, which attempts to free the uninitialized pointer and crashes."
  },
